{
  "format": "ffxi-recomp-builds/1",
  "comment": "Every retail build the recompiler knows: the files it takes (SHA-256 of the retail, packed DLLs), their metadata, and the handful of addresses the runtime and tests name directly. hooks: instructions where host64 steps in (recomp.py --hooks); a build without one lacks that feature. tools/prepare.py picks the build whose FFXiMain.dll hash matches the install; tools/build.py writes these addresses to generated/build.h. Addresses only, no bytes. version: the client version string patch.ver carries (what the lobby's version check sees); 30260805_0 is read from the retail file, 30260903_0 and 30251226_0 follow the same pattern (PE timestamp date) for installs that ship no patch.ver. modern: host/modern.c's menu addresses (Config > Modern and Config > Menus): functions, globals, vtables and menu-table entries; a build without every one of them builds with the feature off. wraps: functions host64 may replace (rt_wrap_*). geometry: the globals runtime/portable/geometry_guest.c reads, and the layout (struct offsets and calling contracts) tests/geometry_replay_test.py verified against the build's own SSE code; a build without it keeps the translated skinning.",
